  "reason": "Commands whose replies hand out something with a remote lifetime: contexts, pages, worlds and remote objects. A reply that arrives after its caller was interrupted, or timed out, is routed to an owner, which adopts or releases it (PROTOCOL.md, Protocol client). `release` names the commands that release it, from the spec's own pairs: Playwright.deleteContext, Playwright.closePage and Runtime.releaseObject. A user world has no release command; it lasts as long as the page.",
